motions.motion_text:
WHEREAS research shows regular physical activity helps reduce the impact of or prevent many chronic diseases, helps prevent premature death, and helps improve quality of life and physical functioning;
AND WHEREAS access to active play in nature and outdoors – with its risks – is essential for healthy child development, including physical and mental well-being;
AND WHEREAS promoting physical activity is part of the Ontario Public Health Standards (OPHS) and aligns with key elements of Ottawa Public Health’s (OPH) 2023-2027 Strategic Plan, the City of Ottawa Official Plan, and the City of Ottawa Transportation Master Plan;
AND WHEREAS Outdoor Play Canada, an Ottawa-based national not-for-profit organization that brings together advocates, practitioners, researchers and partner organizations to promote, protect, and preserve access to play in nature and the outdoors for all people living in Canada, launched the evidence-based 2025 Position Statement on Active Outdoor Play (AOP10) on September 25, 2025;
AND WHEREAS the AOP10 calls for systemic change and includes calls to action for individuals, communities and different sectors which aim to make active outdoor play a fundamental right and sustainable part of societies;
AND WHEREAS OPH staff were present at the Canadian Centre for Outdoor Play for the launch of the AOP10 to show support and make a statement regarding the health benefits of active outdoor play;
AND WHEREAS a formal endorsement by the Board of Health for the City of Ottawa Health Unit:
Can enhance the social norm that active outdoor play is beneficial for health and well-being and;
Can be used by Ottawa Public Health staff as a framework for supporting physical activity policies, training, and infrastructure initiatives with other City of Ottawa departments and external partners;
THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED that the Board of Health for the City of Ottawa Health Unit formally endorse the Outdoor Play Canada 2025 Position Statement on Active Outdoor Play and express its strong support for Ottawa Public Health to work with partners and support changes that advance the individual, population, and community health benefits of active outdoor play;
AND BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Board of Health for the City of Ottawa Health Unit request that its Members, collectively and individually and with support from Ottawa Public Health employees, serve as public health champions by advocating for active outdoor play in accordance with this motion at every opportunity, including at other Boards, at working groups, at standing committees, at sub-committees and at City Council.
